O5. Is 'shape space' the right word?
============================================================================
  scaling the configuration by 0.8: diagram changes by 1.168e-01
  scaling the configuration by 1.25: diagram changes by 2.890e-02
  scaling the configuration by 2.0: diagram changes by 3.299e-02
  So the diagram is NOT scale invariant, and the honest statement is that
  the braid is an invariant of the curve in configuration space modulo
  TRANSLATIONS AND ROTATIONS. The wall locus r_ik = r_jk is separately
  scale invariant, so the walls, but not the diagram, descend to the
  shape sphere.

============================================================================
O6. Is the persistence diagram well posed here?
============================================================================
  rho is a smooth Morse function on the plane decaying to 0.
    maxima 3, merge saddles 2, essential classes 1, all saddles 2
    Morse count  #max - #saddle = 1  (must be 1)
  Superlevel H_0 persistence of such a function is standard, and the
  three classes are exactly the three bodies.

============================================================================
O7. Do the three features stay off the diagonal for the whole loop?
============================================================================
  An order-3 permutation of diagram points needs three features that
  survive the whole circuit, stay distinguishable, and never reach the
  diagonal. Over one T/3 loop, sampled at 600 instants:

    sigma 0.22: features [3], min persistence over the loop 0.4238, min pairwise separation 8.57e-04
    sigma 0.26: features [3], min persistence over the loop 0.2050, min pairwise separation 1.28e-03
    sigma 0.30: features [3], min persistence over the loop 0.0598, min pairwise separation 1.52e-03
    sigma 0.34: features [3], min persistence over the loop 0.0008, min pairwise separation 1.62e-03

  The minimum persistence is bounded well away from zero, so no feature
  approaches the diagonal. The separation touches zero only at the
  isosceles instants, which is where two vines cross.

============================================================================
O8. Is T/3 the PRIMITIVE period in unlabeled configuration space?
============================================================================
  If some shorter time also returned the configuration as a set, the loop
  would not be the primitive one and the order would be wrong.

    times s/T at which the configuration returns as a SET:
      s/T = 0.33333   mismatch 2.98e-08   relabelling [1, 2, 0]
      s/T = 0.66667   mismatch 6.98e-08   relabelling [2, 0, 1]

  The first return is at T/3 with a 3-cycle, so T/3 is primitive and the
  order is 3, not a multiple of something smaller.
